WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.550
Film Courage: I understand you moved to Los
Angeles when you were 27 or 28?&nbsp;Anybody who

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:12.930
is&nbsp;under age 30&nbsp;feels that pressure to make
it. I feel like now even more so [in a culture

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:18.390
of influencers]. Can you share your opinion
on this and what you tell your students?

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.669
Choice Skinner, Actor/Director/Instructor:&nbsp;I’ve
learned the difference between men and women

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:26.109
when it comes to birthdays, it’s really
funny.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:33.820
Every guy has a mental meltdown when their
birthday approaches because they haven’t

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.890
accomplished what they wanted to accomplish
in life.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.809
Women are different. You guys will go out
and you’ll deal with it in a different way.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:43.179
You guys will go shopping, you will buy some
shoes. They’ll work it out, they’ll figure

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:52.519
it out. Guys have a mental meltdown. We can’t
handle it because a man is typically (in his

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:58.820
own mind thinking) judged my his achievements,
by his accomplishments. And we all unfortunately

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.910
do that to ourselves, we plan out our life.
And we hear people say it,&nbsp;I didn’t think

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.430
I’d be here, I thought I’d be so much
further.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:16.250
And for me when I had that epiphany, when
I had that meltdown, I think I went into this

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.480
place of saying to myself&nbsp;Okay, well if that’s
not what’s happening now, what am I supposed

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:27.860
to do?&nbsp;And like I said, you keep going. The
hardest part is to keep going, I think for

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:35.770
most people having that understanding of&nbsp;Okay
life is what it is, it’s not what I want

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:39.570
it to be, it’s what it’s going to be and
I’m okay with that. And am I okay with that?

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.700
Am I okay with being this age and not having
this?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.540
But I did start the entertainment industry
a little later. Kids in my class started in

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.770
their teens and they’re doing great now.
Actors and people that I’ve worked with

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:58.870
when they were 19 and they’re doing phenomenal
now. Big agents and two or three TV shows

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:03.080
and stuff but I firmly believe that if it
wasn’t supposed to happen until 50, it’s

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.201
not going to happen until 50.
So there is nothing you can do about it. And

00:02:06.201 --> 00:02:13.700
to me the growth is accepting it, really,
really, really accepting that. And that’s

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.920
what my epiphany was, it’s like&nbsp;Okay, it’s
not supposed to happen this way. Are you okay

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:24.540
with that?&nbsp;And moving from there. And I think
once people do that, that’s the true level

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:30.500
of faith knowing that this is what you’re
supposed to being doing. There is no falsehood

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.960
in it, it’s just a thing of a matter of
time.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:40.590
Film Courage: What if you’re okay with it
and you’ve worked on yourself but you’re

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:45.880
getting all these little voices from here
and there and it’s your thirtieth birthday

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.350
and…I mean I’m well past thirty but I
remember that pressure.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:54.670
And for me thirty was wonderfully freeing.
I was in a place where I was getting out of

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:59.040
a bad situation so I felt good, but I know
a lot of people are under this weird pressure.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:05.430
Can you talk about this pressure from outside
yourself? What if you’ve worked on yourself

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.880
but outside yourself you are getting pressure?

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.790
Choice:&nbsp;Honestly, I never really had that
pressure. Once…and if it was going to be

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:17.140
it was going to be from my mom because my
mom is one of my driving forces, but she’s

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:21.260
my number one fan, she’s my biggest fan
so it never came to that point.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.570
Now there were always people around accomplishing.
That’s a different pressure that I put on

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:31.241
myself, seeing other people get there and
wondering why I’m not. If anyone says that

00:03:31.241 --> 00:03:35.150
it doesn’t bother them, they’re lying.
That’s the narcissism, that’s who we are

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.330
as actors and entertainers, like we want to
be doing just as great as somebody else. It’s

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:43.849
not competition, it’s just a thing of&nbsp;I’m
talented, this person is talented, I should

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:44.990
be there as well.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:54.760
Life isn’t fair and it ain’t a circus
either. I think once I realized that quote…once

00:03:54.760 --> 00:04:01.250
I realized that…things got easier for me.
So there was never really any outside pressure

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:06.200
for that in regards to me. There was always
fear of&nbsp;Am I going to make it? Am I ever

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.060
going to be able to get there? Am I ever going
to be able to do this?&nbsp;That’s always a

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:14.500
fear because you’re battling life, you’re
battling time. Time is the most precious gift

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:18.019
that is given to you. And you’re hoping
that&nbsp;Man, I’m hoping by the time I’m

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:21.530
this age, I’m going to be able to do this.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.130
But listen, if you’re not doing what you
love, get out and find out what that is.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.121
Film Courage: And if you are doing what you
love and you’re hearing…or even if no

00:04:31.121 --> 00:04:38.020
one is saying it to you but you just turn
on Twitter and see&nbsp;The Top 30 of Age 30 or

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:42.080
25 Under 25, so then the media is telling
you that you’re not okay?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.409
Choice:&nbsp;Yes, but times are different. I mean
back then when I was just acting it was a

00:04:46.409 --> 00:04:51.270
different time than it is now. There are people
in their 60’s and 70’s becoming stars,

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.909
overnight sensations and stuff. Listen I tell
my actors all the time, if your family or

00:04:56.909 --> 00:05:01.319
people are not on your crew then why should
they be there when you finally get blessed

00:05:01.319 --> 00:05:05.719
because it’s going to happen. And I do tell
people the only&nbsp;why&nbsp;it won’t happen is

00:05:05.719 --> 00:05:07.120
if you quit.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:13.650
There’s a definitive thing that happens
if you quit, you don’t make it. It’s night

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:18.550
and day. It’s black and white. You stay
in the game, it’s a number’s game, you

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.819
will get there. Now the level that what you
get to is primarily on your understanding

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:30.550
of the business and how much of what you want
to give over of who you are (your commitment).

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:41.129
But unless your mom or your dad is doing sound
and holding the boom mic and picking up sand

00:05:41.129 --> 00:05:45.509
bags and stuff, they don’t have the right
to say anything about your career if they’re

00:05:45.509 --> 00:05:50.560
not doing that. If they’re really, really
behind you and supporting you, I can understand

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:57.400
hearing their voices. But if they’re not
supporting you by sending money or plane tickets

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.789
when they want you to come home and all that?
Why would you even listen to them honestly?

